/*!
@defgroup semihost Utility semihost - ARM semihosting

ARM semihosting (`BKPT 0xAB`) lets a target use the debugger host's console and
filesystem with no on-target UART. The component has four independent units:

| Kconfig unit | Provides |
|--------------|----------|
| `utility.semihost` | Base host call + direct file API (`SEMIHOST_Open/Read/Seek/Flen/Close`), libc-free |
| `utility.semihost_console` | libc `_write`/`__write`/`fputc` retarget: C `printf` goes to the host |
| `utility.semihost_file` | libc file retarget: `fopen`/`fwrite`/`fread` hit host files |
| `utility.debug_console_semihost` | debug-console backend: the SDK `PRINTF` goes to the host |

Cortex-M (T32) only. On M3/M4/M7 and M33/M55/M85 the component reads
DHCSR.C_DEBUGEN and returns -1 when no debugger is attached; on M0/M0+/M23 DHCSR
is not software-readable, so `BKPT` without a debugger hard-faults - do not ship
semihosting enabled on those cores.

# Console via libc printf

@code
CONFIG_MCUX_COMPONENT_utility.semihost_console=y
@endcode

Call standard `printf`. Flush before exiting (the buffer is line-buffered):

@code
SEMIHOST_ConsoleFlush();
SEMIHOST_Exit(0);
@endcode

This coexists with `utility.debug_console`: the SDK `PRINTF` stays on UART while
C `printf` goes to semihosting. To route existing `PRINTF` sites to semihosting
without code changes, build with `-DSDK_DEBUGCONSOLE=0` and leave
`SDK_DEBUGCONSOLE_UART` undefined - but prefer the debug-console backend below,
which keeps `PRINTF` a function macro and avoids the toolchain `printf`
`-Wformat` checking that `SDK_DEBUGCONSOLE=0` turns on across the whole SDK.

# Console via the debug-console backend

Moves a board's `PRINTF` from UART to semihosting: turn off the board's default
console, then enable this backend.

@code
CONFIG_MCUX_PRJSEG_module.board.console=n        /* disable the board's default console (or console_lite) */
CONFIG_MCUX_COMPONENT_utility.debug_console_semihost=y
@endcode

`PRINTF` becomes `DbgConsole_Printf` (a function, not the toolchain `printf`),
so no UART is linked and no `-Wformat` is triggered. Mutually exclusive with
`debug_console` / `_lite` / `_rtt`.

# Viewing the output

Semihosting I/O is rendered by the debugger, so where it shows up depends on the
tool, not on this component.

Command line (`west debug` → GDB against the probe's gdbserver): enable
semihosting in the session, then pick the output sink.

@code
monitor semihosting enable
monitor semihosting IOClient 1   /* 1 = telnet, 2 = GDB console, 3 = both */
continue
@endcode

- J-Link: `IOClient 1` sends output to the J-Link telnet port (2333).
- LinkServer: output goes to its semihosting telnet port (default 3334, set by
  west's `--semihost-port`); connect a telnet client to read it.

IDE project (`west build -t guiproject`):

| Project | Where the output appears |
|---------|--------------------------|
| IAR EWARM | View > Terminal I/O |
| MCUXpresso IDE | Console view |
| Keil MDK | command-line GDB only (uVision GUI does not service the trap) |

Keil MDK (MicroLib included) works from the command line: flash under J-Link,
then `monitor semihosting enable` in GDB. The uVision GUI does not service the
semihosting trap - it stops at the `BKPT` and creates no host file - so use
command-line GDB there.

# File I/O

Two ways to reach host files:

- **libc retarget** - enable `utility.semihost_file`, then use standard
  `fopen`/`fwrite`/`fread`/`fseek`/`fclose`. IAR needs the Full DLib config
  (`--dlib_config DLib_Config_Full.h`); the default Normal config omits `FILE`.
- **direct API** - call `SEMIHOST_Open`/`Read`/`Seek`/`Flen`/`Close` from the
  base unit. Libc-free and toolchain-independent, no `--dlib_config` needed.

@code
int h = SEMIHOST_Open("out.txt", kSemihost_OpenW);
SEMIHOST_Write(h, buf, n);
SEMIHOST_Close(h);
@endcode

Notes:
- Host files are relative to the debugger's working directory; there is no
  target filesystem.
- `SEMIHOST_Seek` (and `SYS_SEEK`) is absolute from the start; `SEEK_CUR` is
  unsupported on the GCC/IAR libc retarget (no `SYS_TELL`, no tracked position).
- Keep host filenames to 23 characters or fewer: some host debuggers mishandle
  `SYS_OPEN` for longer names (GDB 14.2 appends bytes, GDB 13.2 fails the open).

# Toolchain support

| Toolchain | Console hook | File hooks |
|-----------|--------------|------------|
| armgcc / MCUXpresso (newlib) | `_write` (strong) | `_open`/`_read`/... |
| IAR EWARM (DLib) | `__write` (weak) | `__open`/`__read`/... |
| ARM Compiler / Keil MDK | `fputc` | `_sys_open`/`_sys_read`/... (non-MicroLib only, not CI-verified) |

The console `fputc` and the direct file API issue the semihosting trap
themselves, so they run on Keil MDK, MicroLib included - verified on frdmmcxw23
(armgcc / IAR / MDK). Only the `semihost_file` libc `fopen` retarget needs a
file-system layer MicroLib lacks; use the direct API there.

# Caveats

- Do not call from an ISR: `BKPT` halts the core synchronously.
- The console redirect uses one file-scope buffer and is not reentrant.

# Reference

- ARM Semihosting for AArch32 and AArch64 (Arm DUI 0471).
- `examples/component_examples/semihost` - sample app (console + host file I/O).
*/
